# PostgreSQL / database

Source: [awesome-cursorrules postgresql.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules/blob/main/rules/postgresql.mdc) — this bot uses SQLite by default and Postgres when `DATABASE_URL` is set (`db/` package + `psycopg`).

## Queries

- Parameterized always — never string interpolation into SQL
- Prefer explicit columns over `SELECT *` on large tables
- LIMIT on potentially large result sets

## Schema

- Prefer TIMESTAMPTZ semantics for timestamps when adding Postgres-facing columns
- NOT NULL by default; nullable only when intentional
- Explicit ON DELETE for FKs when introducing relations

## Dual backend

- Changes in `db/` must work for both SQLite and Postgres paths unless the task is VPS-only
- Normalize `postgres://` → `postgresql://` as existing code does
- Do not truncate or drop user data from app code

## Forbidden

- No plaintext secrets in the DB
- No `TRUNCATE` / destructive one-off SQL in handlers
